why Every Alliance quest of Blackrock Depths, with the second run Magni's and Windsor's chains need.

# Blackrock Depths' Alliance quests in one guide: Ironforge, Dun Morogh, the
# Burning Steppes (Morgan's Vigil, Flame Crest, Cyrus), Redridge and
# Stormwind for The True Masters, back to Ironforge and Morgan's Vigil, a
# first run, the hand-ins and The Love Potion's errands in Azshara and
# Un'Goro Crater, a second run, then the last hand-ins. Steps already done are
# passed over, so the guide picks up wherever the chain stands.
#
# The chains:
# - Royal Historian Archesonus' 3702 -> 3701 The Smoldering Ruins of
#   Thaurissan -> King Magni's 4341 Kharan Mighthammer -> Kharan's 4342 ->
#   4361 The Bearer of Bad News -> Magni's 4362 The Fate of the Kingdom
#   (the second run: the Emperor) -> Princess Moira's 4363.
# - Helendis Riverhorn's 4182 Dragonkin Menace -> 4183 -> 4184 -> 4185 ->
#   4186 -> 4223 -> 4224 The True Masters -> Marshal Maxwell's 4241 Marshal
#   Windsor -> Windsor's 4242 Abandoned Hope -> A Crumpled Up Note 4264 (it
#   drops in the second run) -> 4282 A Shred of Hope -> 4322 Jail Break!
# - Ragnar Thunderbrew's 4126 Hurley Blackbreath; Jalinda Sprig's 4262
#   Overmaster Pyron -> 4263 Incendius!; Oralius' 4286 The Good Stuff;
#   Maxwort Uberglint's 4123 The Heart of the Mountain; Cyrus Therepentous'
#   4023 -> 4024 A Taste of Flame; Franclorn Forgewright's 3801 -> 3802 Dark
#   Iron Legacy (the Shadowforge Key); Yuka Screwspigot's 4136 Ribbly
#   Screwspigot.
# - Mistress Nagmara's 4201 The Love Potion (taken inside, handed in on the
#   second run).
#
# Left out: 4295 Rocknot's Ale (repeatable); 4083 The Spectral Chalice (it
# needs the Mining skill); 3911 The Last Element (no giver in the data; the
# Horde's 7201 is the one Vivian Lagrave gives); 7604 A Binding Contract (it
# needs Molten Core); 8933 Just Compensation, 8961 Three Kings of Flame and
# 9015 The Challenge (the Dungeon Set 2 and Valthalak chains); 6402 Stormwind
# Rendezvous after Jail Break! (the Onyxia attunement from there on); the
# breadcrumbs 4324 Yuka Screwspigot from Tanaris and 4128 Ragnar Thunderbrew
# from the Blasted Lands (off this guide's way; their quests open without
# them); 4022 and the Searing Gorge chain before it (4023, the other A Taste
# of Flame, opens 4024 without them); the Thorium Brotherhood's favours
# (repeatable) and the off-page Just Compensation and In Demand quests.
#
# Inside: nothing in the data places the bosses, Marshal Windsor, Kharan,
# Mistress Nagmara, Princess Moira or the Monument of Franclorn Forgewright
# inside, so their goals stand at the door (@34.8,85.3, Searing Gorge) with
# `group 5`. The bosses come in the order of the client's dungeon journal,
# not of a recorded run; every quest goal is counted by the quest log, so a
# group that takes them in another order still gets each step ticked.
#
# Sources (facts only):
# - Quests, NPCs, items, objects and rewards: Polestar's reference data
#   (data/forever, built from QuestieDB Forever 1.1.4) and Polestar 0.4.1.1's
#   Codex page for the dungeon. The Heart of the Mountain's quest needs a
#   Relic Coffer Key, which the Anvilrage dwarves drop; the data names no
#   source for the Heart itself. Cyrus's Frenzied Black Drake drops the
#   Black Dragonflight Molt. Lint warns that the door is more than 50 yards
#   from the fanny packs' droppers outside; the goal stays at the door for
#   the ones inside.
# - The door: QuestieDB's list of Forever's dungeons, as Polestar's Codex holds it
#   (data/codex/entrances.json).
# - The dungeon's size, levels and bosses: the client's group finder and
#   dungeon journal, as Polestar's Codex page holds them (five players, levels
#   52 to 60).
# INGAME: where inside do Marshal Windsor, Kharan, Mistress Nagmara, the
#   Monument and the Heart of the Mountain stand?

